  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Carnival tradition of Recife and the Pernambuco Zona da Mata in which groups costumed as Indigenous warriors dance in rows to a small terno; IPHAN has registered it as Brazilian cultural heritage. The terno combines a small cane pipe (gaita), a shaker (caracaxá) and a bass drum, while the dancers click wooden bow-and-arrow preacás in rhythm. The credited bamboo-flute card stands in for the gaita, the surdo for the bass drum, a source-unspecified shaker for the caracaxá and palitos for the preacás.",
